===Etymology===
From {{w|James Alfred Van Allen}}, US [[physicist]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=Van Allen [[radiation belt]]}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy|physics}} Either of two [[torus]]-shaped areas of high-energy [[charge]]d [[particle]]s which partly [[surround]] [[Earth]], trapped by its [[magnetic field]]. The areas are characterised by intense [[radiation]]. When the belts "overload", particles strike the upper atmosphere and [[fluoresce]], causing the [[polar]] [[aurora]].

